{
    "station_schema": 9,
    "name": "Conveyor Showcase — PhysX Range",
    "conveyor_simulation_mode": "logical",
    "_comment": [
        "Five separated demonstrations use the built-in roller conveyor asset.",
        "All spawners clone the single hidden Box workpiece station object; product shape is not hardcoded in the conveyor.",
        "The far negative-Z line is a covered 100 mm-pitch PhysX belt demonstration.",
        "The negative-Z line is a PhysX two-turn ascending spiral using 100 mm pitch.",
        "The center PhysX line transitions from 100 mm pitch to a 70 mm-pitch incline and back.",
        "The positive-Z spiral remains logical as an explicit backend comparison.",
        "The far positive-Z line is a 120 mm coarse-pitch PhysX lane carrying the shared box workpiece.",
        "PhysX products are dropped onto generated rollers and move only through contact friction.",
        "All touching conveyor interfaces share all four mounting centers exactly.",
        "Schema 7 parameter_links bind every touching end/start deck-height pair bidirectionally."
    ],
